GitHub / Git Cheat Sheet
Repository basics
git clone <repo-url>          # Clone a repository
git init                      # Create a new Git repo
git remote -v                 # Show remote URLs
git remote add origin <url>   # Add remote
git remote set-url origin <url>

Daily workflow
git status                    # Check changes
git add <file>                # Stage a file
git add .                     # Stage all changes
git commit -m "message"       # Commit
git push                      # Push commits
git pull                      # Fetch + merge remote changes

Branches
git branch                    # List branches
git branch <name>             # Create branch
git switch <name>             # Switch branch
git switch -c <name>          # Create + switch
git push -u origin <name>     # Push new branch
git branch -d <name>          # Delete local branch
git push origin --delete <name> # Delete remote branch

Undo changes
git restore <file>            # Discard unstaged changes
git restore --staged <file>   # Unstage file
git reset --soft HEAD~1       # Undo commit, keep changes staged
git reset HEAD~1              # Undo commit, keep changes
git revert <commit>           # Safely undo a commit

Inspect history
git log                       # Commit history
git log --oneline             # Compact history
git show <commit>             # Show commit details
git diff                      # Unstaged changes
git diff --staged             # Staged changes

GitHub CLI (gh)
gh auth login                # Log into GitHub
gh repo create               # Create repository
gh repo clone <owner/repo>   # Clone GitHub repo
gh repo view                 # View repository
gh repo fork <owner/repo>    # Fork repository

gh pr create                 # Create pull request
gh pr list                   # List PRs
gh pr view <number>          # View PR
gh pr checkout <number>      # Check out PR
gh pr merge <number>         # Merge PR

gh issue create              # Create issue
gh issue list                # List issues
